<p>+1</p>
<p>The final note really sealed the deal for me. And here's why:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'm not sure if you meant it this way, but by adding:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Naturally, none of this goes in the official SCP file. The totally hypothetical one, of course.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You've got sort of a double meaning here. This could read as, &quot;None of this goes in the SCP file, which as we all know is hypothetical anyway, wink wink.&quot; This <em>could</em> also read as, &quot;None of this goes in the SCP file, but of course it goes in the fake hypothetical file.&quot;</p>
<p>Which, since we are reading this in an SCP file, would imply that the whole article we've just read is fake, and there is no cheeseburger, but there is something else with similar attributes requiring similar containment procedures.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>As scarhaver mentioned above, it's kind of a mental riddle, and I guess I really like that.</p>

